    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with a high-efficiency floor, led by **Cal Raleigh** (78.01) and **Lawrence Butler** (73.50), who represent our strongest individual plays. **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a massive +19% boost due to the favorable matchup against Kay, with his spot in the #2 hole maximizing his potential for counting stats. Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** is poised to exploit a high-park-factor environment; his +13% platoon adjustment is the engine behind his elite score, making him a high-upside play despite batting in the bottom third of the order. **Taylor Ward** (68.38) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.33) also provide excellent stability, with the latter remaining a vital asset in our SB-heavy strategy despite a slight efficiency penalty for facing a pitcher with a solid hold rate.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Bryson Stott**, who remains the primary bench option at 48.41. While **Bryson Stott** offers some upside against Freeland, he was relegated to the bench because his dynamic platoon split (L) against a lefty neutralized the gains from his stolen base potential. The marginal score of 49.21 for **Matt Chapman** is largely buoyed by the wind-out conditions at the stadium, yet we remain cautious about his matchup against Braxton Ashcraft. We are closely monitoring the lineup security for **Luis Arraez** and **Jung Hoo Lee** against that same arm; while their scores are bolstered by high-order placement and wind, the -11% SP skill penalty suggests they will have to work hard for their production. With **Yainer Diaz** still sidelined on the IL, our current configuration maximizes our daily efficiency, though we are wary of any late-day weather shifts that could impact the wind-aided offensive environment.",
